1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,300
Nine thousand eight hundred fifty dollars.

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:04,410
Or two hundred eighty-three.

3
00:00:04,460 --> 00:00:06,730
Same surgery. Same hospital.

4
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:09,670
Same year. The difference is which card

5
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:10,540
is in your wallet…

6
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:12,830
and one of those two cards comes with a

7
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:15,060
door that only opens one way.

8
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,540
This is The Fine Print.

9
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,850
By the end you'll know three things.

10
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:22,430
What the two cards cost in a bad year,

11
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:23,500
run on screen.

12
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:25,810
The rule that makes switching between them

13
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:27,690
a one-way door for most people.

14
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:30,350
And the order to do things in, if you're

15
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,950
thinking about walking through it before

16
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,590
December seventh. This is education, not

17
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:37,080
advice. Nobody here sells insurance.

18
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:40,050
Start with the bad year, because that's

19
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:41,370
the one that moves the money.

20
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:44,270
A Medicare Advantage plan is Medicare delivered

21
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:47,010
by a private insurer, usually with a network,

22
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:49,090
often for zero dollars a month.

23
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:50,930
Every plan has a cap…

24
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:53,490
the most you can pay for covered in-network

25
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:54,590
care in a year.

26
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:57,010
For twenty twenty-seven, Medicare lets

27
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:59,430
that cap go as high as nine thousand eight

28
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:00,570
hundred fifty dollars.

29
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:01,830
That's the ceiling.

30
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:04,230
The plans you're looking at this fall each

31
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:05,650
pick a number under it.

32
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:08,090
Original Medicare with a supplement works

33
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:09,110
the other way around.

34
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:12,310
Medigap, the supplement, is a private policy

35
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,310
that pays what Medicare doesn't.

36
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:17,390
Plan G, the most popular one, pays everything

37
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:20,550
Medicare approves… except the Part B deductible.

38
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:23,050
Two hundred eighty-three dollars for twenty

39
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:25,290
twenty-six. The twenty twenty-seven figure

40
00:01:25,340 --> 00:01:26,390
comes out in November.

41
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:28,150
So picture a gauge.

42
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:30,590
Twelve months, and the needle climbs with

43
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:33,270
every copay. On the Advantage plan it can

44
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:35,250
climb all the way to the red line.

45
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:38,430
On Plan G it stops at two hundred eighty-three.

46
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:41,170
For that, you pay a premium every month,

47
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:42,590
healthy or not.

48
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:46,270
Medigap prices vary by state, by age, by

49
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:48,570
company. Say one hundred fifty dollars

50
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,790
a month on the low end, two hundred twenty

51
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:51,650
on the high end.

52
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:54,010
The real range for your zip code is on

53
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:55,260
Medicare dot gov.

54
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:56,970
Here's the bad year.

55
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:58,810
Advantage plan at the ceiling…

56
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:00,990
nine thousand eight hundred fifty.

57
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:04,130
Plan G at one fifty a month: twelve months

58
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:06,530
of premiums, eighteen hundred, plus the

59
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:08,810
deductible. Two thousand eighty-three.

60
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:11,510
At two twenty a month, two thousand nine

61
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:14,250
hundred twenty-three. Here's the good year.

62
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:17,490
Advantage: a few copays, call it six hundred

63
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:20,430
dollars. Plan G: the same two thousand

64
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:22,870
eighty-three. The supplement costs more

65
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:24,270
in the years nothing happens.

66
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,390
That's the trade.

67
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:28,350
You pay every month so the bad year can't

68
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,150
reach your savings.

69
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,770
Run ten years, two of them bad.

70
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:34,730
Advantage: eight good years at six hundred,

71
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,180
two at the ceiling…

72
00:02:36,730 --> 00:02:38,470
twenty-four thousand five hundred.

73
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:42,130
Plan G at one fifty: twenty thousand eight

74
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:45,210
hundred thirty. At two twenty: twenty-nine

75
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:46,630
thousand two hundred thirty.

76
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:50,390
It's close. On money alone, over a decade,

77
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,930
it's roughly a wash.

78
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:55,230
Either way it's about two years of a twelve-thousand-dollar

79
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:56,290
draw from savings.

80
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:58,370
The difference is whether you know when

81
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:00,890
it comes… which tells you the real difference

82
00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:02,230
was never the price.

83
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:03,870
How to check yours.

84
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:06,350
Open your plan's Evidence of Coverage,

85
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:09,230
find the line that says maximum out-of-pocket,

86
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:10,630
and write the number down.

87
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:12,880
That's your red line for next year.

88
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:16,250
The real difference is which choice you

89
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:17,100
can take back.

90
00:03:17,540 --> 00:03:20,030
Advantage to Advantage, every fall.

91
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:22,830
Supplement to Advantage, every fall.

92
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:24,910
Advantage back to a supplement…

93
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,350
that's the door.

94
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:29,530
Federal law gives you two guaranteed openings.

95
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:32,230
The first is a six-month window that starts

96
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:34,310
the month you're sixty-five and on Part

97
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:36,790
B. The second is a trial right.

98
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:39,050
If you joined an Advantage plan for the

99
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:41,190
first time, you can leave within the first

100
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:43,210
twelve months and buy a supplement with

101
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:44,290
no health questions.

102
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:47,290
After that, in most states, the supplement

103
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:48,870
company can ask about your health.

104
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,310
It can charge you more.

105
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,690
It can make you wait up to six months on

106
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:54,130
a condition you already have.

107
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:56,030
Or it can say no.

108
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:58,110
How many people does that touch?

109
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:00,490
The Kaiser Family Foundation looked at

110
00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:03,310
it this month, October twenty twenty-six.

111
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:05,550
Seventy-four percent of people on Medicare

112
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:08,250
Advantage… about twenty point nine million…

113
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:10,470
have a condition that could get a supplement

114
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:12,040
application turned down.

115
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:15,380
Three out of four.

116
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,190
There are exceptions, and they matter.

117
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:21,090
If your plan leaves Medicare or stops serving

118
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:23,190
your county, you get a guaranteed right

119
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:25,990
to a supplement, Plan G included, as long

120
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:28,090
as you apply within sixty-three days of

121
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:28,950
the coverage ending.

122
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,390
For twenty twenty-six, that letter went

123
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:33,670
to about two point nine million people,

124
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:36,970
a tenfold increase in two years, by a study

125
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:38,690
published in JAMA in February.

126
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:41,350
If that letter is on your table, it isn't

127
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:42,350
only bad news.

128
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,490
It's a key.

129
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:45,730
And a handful of states write their own

130
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:48,470
rules. Connecticut and New York take supplement

131
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:51,350
applications year-round, no health questions.

132
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:54,070
Massachusetts and Maine open a window once

133
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,750
a year. Sixteen states have what's called

134
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:57,870
a birthday rule…

135
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,490
but read that one carefully.

136
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:01,870
It lets people who already have a supplement

137
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:03,030
switch to another one.

138
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:05,440
It does not open the door from Advantage.

139
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,050
How to check yours.

140
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:09,450
Call your State Health Insurance Assistance

141
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:13,170
Program, free, no sales, and ask one question.

142
00:05:13,220 --> 00:05:15,570
Do I have a guaranteed-issue right this

143
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:18,360
fall, and which situation gives it to me?

144
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:22,290
If you've decided to walk through, the

145
00:05:22,340 --> 00:05:24,010
order matters more than the date.

146
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:26,350
First, the supplement application.

147
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,390
Before you cancel anything.

148
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:31,230
Get the yes in writing, with a start date

149
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:32,350
of January first.

150
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:34,310
You can apply while you're still on the

151
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:36,890
Advantage plan. The policy just can't start

152
00:05:36,940 --> 00:05:38,110
until the plan ends.

153
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:40,230
Second, the drug plan.

154
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:42,730
Original Medicare has no drug coverage

155
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:45,610
built in. You pick a Part D plan by December

156
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:47,710
seventh, or there's a penalty later.

157
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:50,890
Third, and only then, let the Advantage

158
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:53,790
plan go. Enrolling in the stand-alone drug

159
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:55,350
plan does that for you.

160
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:57,550
Do it in the other order, and you can end

161
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,930
up on Original Medicare with no supplement,

162
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:02,470
holding a form that asks about your health.

163
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:05,090
So the question this fall was never which

164
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:06,090
card is cheaper.

165
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:08,520
Over ten years, the money is close.

166
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:11,350
The question is which decision you can

167
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:13,080
still undo at seventy-five…

168
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:15,670
because one of them, for three people out

169
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,610
of four, you can't.

170
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:20,810
A fee-only fiduciary or a CPA can run your

171
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:22,910
own numbers, and the State Health Insurance

172
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:24,730
Assistance Program will walk you through

173
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:25,810
the rules for free.

174
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:28,190
New numbers every Tuesday and Friday.

175
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:30,580
Subscribe so the next one finds you.

176
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:33,920
Will your money last as long as you do?
